5, "rotation": 0, "text": ["At a global level, coal is the dominant fuel for power generation, however its share fell 1.3 percentage points to 35.1% in 2020, the lowest level in our data series. The share of renewables rose to record levels last year (11.7%), with the combined share of renewables and gas-fired power (35.1%) equalling coal for the first time. Europe's share of renewables in power generation reached 23.8%, surpassing nuclear energy and making Europe the first region where renewables are the dominant source of power generation."]}, "id": "3G5GX7P879", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 31.04253112033195, "y": 89.41908713692946, "width": 38.511410788381745, "height": 3.941908713692939, "rotation": 0}, "id": "Sl6aaqNiq4", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 31.04253112033195, "y": 89.41908713692946, "width": 38.511410788381745, "height": 3.941908713692939, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "Sl6aaqNiq4", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 31.04253112033195, "y": 89.41908713692946, "width": 38.511410788381745, "height": 3.941908713692939, "rotation": 0, "text": ["BP Statistical Review of World Energy, June 2021"]}, "id": "Sl6aaqNiq4", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 21.473029045643152, "y": 82.98755186721992, "width": 17.855290456431533, "height": 3.526970954356841, "rotation": 0}, "id": "14IDXVdogK", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 1920,